                        "entry_id": "5003fe07-1af4-3eaa-ad9d-6fa09783b965",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Including all aspects of; encompassing."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "baf49bb7-8463-313e-ae0d-8dc7795b5dd8",
                        "entry_id": "5003fe07-1af4-3eaa-ad9d-6fa09783b965",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Surrounding."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c18fce88-5e1f-4d8e-87c2-6b3e02f04eea",
                                "sense_id": "baf49bb7-8463-313e-ae0d-8dc7795b5dd8",
                                "text": "Thus gaiety and cheerfulness prevail, / Spreading from young to old, from old to young, / And no one seems to want his share.—Immense / Is the recess, the circumambient world / Magnificent, by which they are embraced: […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "92203124-0530-4554-a453-7ee3c66facae",
                                "sense_id": "baf49bb7-8463-313e-ae0d-8dc7795b5dd8",
                                "text": "Philip seemed really to be born again. He breathed the circumambient air as though he had never breathed it before, and he took a child's pleasure in all the facts of the world."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7a71bef4-0d00-456a-b9b2-89ae1cfbf3b0",
                                "sense_id": "baf49bb7-8463-313e-ae0d-8dc7795b5dd8",
                                "text": "Groups of citizens—broad-browed Roman colonists and coarse-haired Romanised natives, together with obvious hybrids of the two strains, alike clad in cheap woollen togas—and sprinklings of helmeted legionaries and coarse-mantled, black-bearded tribesmen of the circumambient Vascones—all thronged the few paved streets and forum; moved by some vague and ill-defined uneasiness."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5c33c637-4e26-403c-a321-1c04fcf66d14",
                                "sense_id": "baf49bb7-8463-313e-ae0d-8dc7795b5dd8",
                                "text": "The growling circumambient toils of London around them fadedbefore the calm of these innocent precincts."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
